        907,
        434
      ],
      "margin_number": 198,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "You have already met present imperatives (active -ε -ετε, middle -ου -εσθε). These are based on the present stem (18). There are also imperatives based (do you ever get that déjà vu feeling?) on the aorist stem, first and second. Their forms are as follows:",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        452,
        186,
        601,
        202
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "First aorist imperatives active and middle",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "box",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        481,
        186,
        633,
        638
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Active (-[σ]ον, -[σ]α-τε)\n2s. παῦσ-ον ‘stop!’\n2pl. παύσα-τε ‘stop!’\nMiddle (-[σ]-αι, -[σ]-ασθε)\n2s. παῦσα-ι ‘cease!’\n2pl. παύσα-σθε ‘cease!’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
